  "published": "2026-11-01T21:14:45.47Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Vendors Swiper 14.4.0 (was 14.0.6) and exposes the parameters 14.3.0 added: LazyPreload, and FadeEffect.Mode with the new out-in transition. Fixes programmatic moves in cssMode: a new move replaces the one in flight instead of racing it, scroll-snap is always handed back, and the animation clock starts on the second frame so a host re-rendering on the same event still sees the move animate. A cssMode slider resized while it rests or moves stays on its slide: Swiper 14.4.0 fixes its own resize handling (https://github.com/nolimits4web/swiper/pull/8250), and an instant SlideTo in cssMode now goes through Swiper's slideTo, so that handling keeps it too. SlideTo in cssMode is now turned down while the slider is disabled or locked in that direction (AllowSlideNext, AllowSlidePrev), as it always was outside cssMode. AttachEvents on a slider whose events are already attached no longer doubles Swiper's listeners.",
